<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ame Pal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1380</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ame Pal was a Tibetan warrior who around 1380 unified the upper Kali Gandaki valley and founded the kingdom of Lo, now Mustang in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>. He is credited with founding the walled capital Lo Manthang, and his descendants ruled Lo until the monarchy was abolished in 2008.</p></div>
